X: 1
T: Allons Danser Colinda
O: Traditional Cajun, Louisiana
N: A two-step whose name probably comes from the calinda, a dance brought to
N: Louisiana from the Caribbean. Still danced at Mardi Gras.
N: Melody from the Fiddler's Companion (from Larry Miller), written there in
N: 8/4; here each 8/4 bar is split into two 4/4 bars. Chords derived from the
N: melody. Transposed down a fifth from C.
L: 1/8
Q: 1/4=130
M: 4/4
K: F
